#usda 1.0
(
    doc = """DEADFALL DEPOT module: physics. Owned by one specialist agent - do not edit from another module.

GENERATED BY tools/gen_physics.py - edit that, re-run it, do not hand-patch this file.

BRIEF section 7 is a three-part deliverable and all three parts are here:

  1. AUTHORED UsdPhysics. One PhysicsScene, 17 PhysicsMaterialAPI looks with real
     friction/restitution/density, 2527 static colliders authored as `over` prims onto
     10_terrain and 20_architecture (never editing those files), 149 settled dynamic
     rigid bodies with RigidBodyAPI + MassAPI, four collision groups and the joints.

  2. A REAL SOLVE. pybullet (tools venv) built the collision world out of these same
     authored colliders - the terrain ground meshes as a concave triangle mesh, the
     architecture as boxes - then dropped every dynamic prop from 5-15 cm above its
     intended surface with a random yaw, a random tilt and a nudge toward the surface
     it should end up against, then ran 14 s at 240 Hz with three energy-bleed
     passes and a damped freeze. Every translate and orient under
     /World/Physics/SettledDebris is a solver result, not a hand value; nothing
     floats and nothing is buried because nothing was placed by hand. The same
     collision world then audited all 887 props in 30_props for ground contact.

  3. PLAUSIBILITY. The drop sites are where junk actually collects in a yard: against
     the warehouse kerb, at the foot of the dock face, washed south out of the hero
     gate, in the service-road ruts, out of the fuel-bund entry gap, and stacked under
     the mezzanine. Drums that came to rest on their sides did so in the solver.

  NOTE: ovrtx renders, it does not simulate (BRIEF s2). Nothing moves at render time.
  This layer is the representation a game engine consumes plus the baked rest state.

  KEEP-OUT: every drop site was rejection-sampled against the LAYOUT s6 cover schedule
  and the five objective points, so this layer never lands on top of 30_props.

  30_props CONTACT AUDIT: 884 props audited, 464 found off their surface,
  221 fixed with a Z-only over (max 248 mm). Section 6 lists what was left alone
  and why. 30_props.usda is not edited by this layer -- only overridden.

  SOLVER AUDIT (printed by the generator, reproduced here so it can be checked):
    bodies dropped           149
    bodies baked into USD    149
    rejected as unsettled    0   (no resting contact, or penetrating >35 mm)
    fastest residual speed   0.74 cm/s   (0 bodies above 1 cm/s)
    floating (no contact)    0
    fewest contact points    3   (every baked body touches something)
    came to rest on its side 71

  All four usdPhysicsValidators (ColliderChecker, RigidBodyChecker,
  PhysicsJointChecker, ArticulationChecker) report 0 errors on the composed stage.
"""
    metersPerUnit = 1
    upAxis = "Z"
)

over "World"
{
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 1. SIMULATION SCENE
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    def PhysicsScene "PhysicsScene"
    {
        vector3f physics:gravityDirection = (0, 0, -1)
        float physics:gravityMagnitude = 9.81
    }

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 2. PHYSICS MATERIALS
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    def Scope "PhysicsMaterials"
    {
        # UsdPhysics binds friction through UsdShadeMaterial prims, so each of these
        # is a real Material. They are bound only at the `physics` purpose, so no
        # renderer ever evaluates them; the surface output exists purely so the
        # material is well formed. Visual looks live in 50_materials.usda.
        # power-trowelled interior slab, sealed
        def Material "PM_ConcreteDry" (
            prepend apiSchemas = ["PhysicsMaterialAPI"]
        )
        {
            float physics:staticFriction = 0.75
            float physics:dynamicFriction = 0.62
            float physics:restitution = 0.05
            float physics:density = 2400
            token outputs:surface.connect = </World/PhysicsMaterials/PM_ConcreteDry/Surface.outputs:surface>
            token outputs:mdl:surface.connect = </World/PhysicsMaterials/PM_ConcreteDry/Surface.outputs:surface>

            def Shader "Surface"
            {
                uniform token info:id = "UsdPreviewSurface"
                float inputs:roughness = 1
                float inputs:metallic = 0
                token outputs:surface
            }
        }
        # rain-soaked dock/apron concrete
        def Material "PM_ConcreteWet" (
            prepend apiSchemas = ["PhysicsMaterialAPI"]
        )
        {
            float physics:staticFriction = 0.48
